cerberus (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add optional Codex CLI vulnerability analysis enrichment.
  * Keep Codex disabled by default and preserve scanner severity as authoritative.
  * Add strict JSON validation, sanitized subprocess environment, read-only sandbox request,
    output-size limits, timeout handling, and SQLite analysis caching.
  * Render validated contextual risk, confidence, reachability, evidence, limitations, and
    recommendations in alert and digest emails.

 -- Cerberus Maintainers <maintainers@example.net>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 16:20:26 +0200

cerberus (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Separate npm runtime and development audit findings in digests.
  * Group duplicate digest findings by evidence while preserving affected targets.
  * Add semver-major npm fix warnings and scoped recommendations.

